From 7d87d4d4df0424484b513ccd9b90c0d799a6f006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiaoliang Yang <xiaoliang.yang_1@nxp.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jul 2024 11:12:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] preempt_rt: allow readers before writer lock acquisition

Allow readers to read as long as the writer has not completely acquired
the semaphore for write. Without this code, the system can hang when an
ENETC interface sends a large number of packets with PREEMPT_RT enabled.

This is NXP Real-Time Edge commit
7d87d4d4df0424484b513ccd9b90c0d799a6f006, which applies cleanly to the
MYIR Linux 6.18.37 kernel.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NXP ENETC PREEMPT_RT integration]
Signed-off-by: Xiaoliang Yang <xiaoliang.yang_1@nxp.com>
Signed-off-by: Hou Zhiqiang <Zhiqiang.Hou@nxp.com>
---
 kernel/locking/rwbase_rt.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/locking/rwbase_rt.c b/kernel/locking/rwbase_rt.c
index 9f4322c07486..428b6962a8d3 100644
--- a/kernel/locking/rwbase_rt.c
+++ b/kernel/locking/rwbase_rt.c
@@ -75,6 +75,17 @@ static int __sched __rwbase_read_lock(struct rwbase_rt *rwb,
 	rwbase_pre_schedule();
 	raw_spin_lock_irq(&rtm->wait_lock);
 
+	/*
+	 * Allow readers, as long as the writer has not completely
+	 * acquired the semaphore for write.
+	 */
+	if (atomic_read(&rwb->readers) != WRITER_BIAS) {
+		atomic_inc(&rwb->readers);
+		raw_spin_unlock_irq(&rtm->wait_lock);
+		rwbase_post_schedule();
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Call into the slow lock path with the rtmutex->wait_lock
 	 * held, so this can't result in the following race:
